sources.body:
Spring Framework provides first-class CORS support. CORS must be processed before Spring Security because preflight requests don't contain cookies (e.g., JSESSIONID). Without proper ordering, Spring Security rejects unauthenticated preflight requests.

[Method 1: CorsConfigurationSource Bean — 자동 감지]
Spring Security automatically configures CORS when a UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource bean is present:
```java
@Bean
UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource corsConfigurationSource() {
    CorsConfiguration configuration = new CorsConfiguration();
    configuration.setAllowedOrigins(Arrays.asList("https://example.com"));
    configuration.setAllowedMethods(Arrays.asList("GET","POST"));
    UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource source = new UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource();
    source.registerCorsConfiguration("/**", configuration);
    return source;
}
```

[Method 2: Spring MVC Integration — withDefaults()]
If Spring MVC CORS support is already configured, Spring Security can use it automatically:
```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class WebSecurityConfig {
    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            // if Spring MVC is on classpath and no CorsConfigurationSource is provided,
            // Spring Security will use CORS configuration provided to Spring MVC
            .cors(withDefaults())
            ...
        return http.build();
    }
}
```

[Method 3: Per-Chain Configuration — 체인별 개별 지정]
For multiple SecurityFilterChain instances:
```java
@Bean
@Order(0)
public SecurityFilterChain apiFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
    http
        .securityMatcher("/api/**")
        .cors((cors) -> cors
            .configurationSource(apiConfigurationSource())
        )
        ...
    return http.build();
}
```

[중요 경고]
1. CORS must be processed BEFORE Spring Security: preflight requests don't contain cookies (like JSESSIONID). If Spring Security processes first, it rejects the unauthenticated request.
2. Do NOT configure both configurationSource and preFlightRequestHandler on the same CorsConfigurer—this causes a startup error.
3. Using .cors(CorsConfigurer::disable) removes Spring Security's CORS support but does NOT prevent browser CORS errors. To fix CORS issues, you must ENABLE CORS support and provide an appropriate configuration source — disabling does nothing useful.

현재 문서 버전: Spring Security 7.1.0 / 6.5.11

Spring MVC provides built-in CORS support through multiple configuration mechanisms.

[1. @CrossOrigin — 컨트롤러/메서드 레벨]
```java
@CrossOrigin(origins = "https://domain2.com", maxAge = 3600)
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/account")
public class AccountController { ... }
```
기본값: 모든 오리진 허용, 모든 헤더 허용, 해당 메서드 매핑, allowCredentials=disabled, maxAge=30분.

[2. Global Configuration — WebMvcConfigurer]
```java
@Configuration
public class WebConfiguration implements WebMvcConfigurer {
    @Override
    public void addCorsMappings(CorsRegistry registry) {
        registry.addMapping("/api/**")
            .allowedOrigins("https://domain1.com", "https://domain2.com")
            .allowedMethods("GET", "PUT")
            .allowedHeaders("header1", "header2", "header3")
            .exposedHeaders("header1", "header2")
            .allowCredentials(true)
            .maxAge(3600);
    }
}
```

[3. CorsFilter — 서블릿 필터 레벨]
```java
CorsConfiguration config = new CorsConfiguration();
config.setAllowCredentials(true);
config.addAllowedOrigin("https://domain1.com");
config.addAllowedHeader("*");
config.addAllowedMethod("*");
UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource source = new UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource();
source.registerCorsConfiguration("/**", config);
CorsFilter filter = new CorsFilter(source);
```
Note: If using Spring Security, it has built-in CORS support, so consider using that instead of CorsFilter.

[핵심 제약 — allowCredentials + wildcard]
When allowCredentials is enabled:
- Wildcards ("*") are NOT authorized in allowOrigins
- Use allowOriginPatterns property to match dynamic origins instead
- Example: .allowOriginPatterns("https://*.domain.com")

[처리 순서/우선순위]
1. Global HandlerMapping level configuration (URL pattern 전체)
2. @CrossOrigin class-level annotations (해당 클래스 모든 메서드)
3. @CrossOrigin method-level annotations (가장 구체적, class-level 덮어쓰기)
4. Custom CorsConfigurationSource implementations

[중요] Spring Security 사용 시: @CrossOrigin 이나 WebMvcConfigurer 만으로는 부족하다 — Spring Security의 필터 체인이 MVC 핸들러보다 먼저 동작하기 때문에 Security 레벨에서도 cors()를 활성화해야 한다.

minimalWorkingConfig.code:
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            .cors(Customizer.withDefaults()) // CorsConfigurationSource 빈을 자동 사용
            .csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable()) // REST API 의 경우
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            );
        return http.build();
    }

    @Bean
    public CorsConfigurationSource corsConfigurationSource() {
        CorsConfiguration configuration = new CorsConfiguration();
        configuration.setAllowedOrigins(Arrays.asList("http://localhost:3000"));
        configuration.setAllowedMethods(Arrays.asList("GET","POST","PUT","DELETE","OPTIONS"));
        configuration.setAllowedHeaders(Arrays.asList("*"));
        configuration.setAllowCredentials(true);
        // allowedOrigins("*") + allowCredentials(true) 조합 금지 → allowedOriginPatterns 사용
        // configuration.setAllowedOriginPatterns(Arrays.asList("*"));
        UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource source = new UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource();
        source.registerCorsConfiguration("/**", configuration);
        return source;
    }
}

